[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-005-cqrs-pattern.md#2-query-logic-in-commands]

#### 2. Query Logic in Commands

**Problem**: Mixing query logic into command handlers

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Query in command handler
public async Task Handle(ProcessClaimCommand cmd)
{
    var provider = await queryDb.Providers
        .Include(p => p.Remittances)
        .Include(p => p.PaymentHistory) // Complex query
        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(p => p.Id == cmd.ProviderId);

    // Business logic...
}
```

**Solution**: Commands only use write model, queries use read model

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Command uses write model only
public async Task Handle(ProcessClaimCommand cmd)
{
    var provider = await writeDb.Providers.FindAsync(cmd.ProviderId); // Simple lookup
    // Business logic...
}
```

