[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-005-cqrs-pattern.md#4-missing-idempotency-in-projections]

#### 4. Missing Idempotency in Projections

**Problem**: Projection services not handling duplicate events

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Non-idempotent projection
public async Task Handle(ClaimProcessedEvent evt)
{
    await readDb.ExecuteSqlAsync(
        "UPDATE ProviderStats SET ClaimCount = ClaimCount + 1 WHERE ProviderId = {0}",
        evt.ProviderId
    ); // Duplicate event = incorrect count
}
```

**Solution**: Idempotent projections using event IDs

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Idempotent projection
public async Task Handle(ClaimProcessedEvent evt)
{
    if (await processedEvents.ContainsAsync(evt.EventId))
        return; // Already processed

    await readDb.ExecuteSqlAsync(
        "UPDATE ProviderStats SET ClaimCount = ClaimCount + 1 WHERE ProviderId = {0}",
        evt.ProviderId
    );

    await processedEvents.AddAsync(evt.EventId);
}
```

