#### HIPAA Compliance for Dual Data Models

CQRS implementations handling Protected Health Information (PHI) must ensure compliance across both write and read models:

**Write Model HIPAA Requirements**:

| Requirement | Implementation | Verification |
|-------------|----------------|--------------|
| **Access Controls** | Role-based access for commands, MFA for sensitive operations | Audit logs showing authentication/authorization |
| **Audit Trail** | Complete audit log of all write operations with user, timestamp, data changed | Command history table, immutable event log |
| **Encryption at Rest** | TDE (Transparent Data Encryption) for write database | SQL Server TDE enabled, encryption verified |
| **Encryption in Transit** | TLS 1.2+ for all database connections | Connection strings enforce encryption |
| **Data Integrity** | ACID transactions, checksums, foreign key constraints | Transaction logs, referential integrity checks |
| **Minimum Necessary** | Commands only access required data fields | Code reviews, least-privilege queries |

**Read Model HIPAA Requirements**:

| Requirement | Implementation | Verification |
|-------------|----------------|--------------|
| **Access Controls** | Same RBAC as write model, query-level authorization | Authorization middleware, integration tests |
| **Audit Trail** | Log all PHI access (who, what, when) | Query audit logs with correlation to users |
| **Encryption at Rest** | TDE for SQL read models, encryption for document stores | Encryption configuration for all read databases |
| **Encryption in Transit** | TLS 1.2+ for all connections | Network traffic inspection, SSL certificate validation |
| **Data Minimization** | Read models only contain fields needed for specific queries | Schema reviews, projection logic audits |
| **Cache Security** | Encrypt cached PHI, short TTLs (≤5 minutes) | Redis encryption enabled, cache policy review |

**Event Bus HIPAA Requirements**:

| Requirement | Implementation | Verification |
|-------------|----------------|--------------|
| **Message Encryption** | Encrypt event payloads containing PHI | Message serialization includes encryption |
| **Access Controls** | Service identity authentication, topic-level authorization | Azure RBAC, service principal permissions |
| **Audit Logging** | Log event publication and consumption | Event bus audit logs, correlation IDs |
| **Message Retention** | Retain events for 7 years (HIPAA requirement) | Event store backup policy, compliance audits |

**Projection Lag and Data Currency**:
- Document acceptable lag for PHI queries (e.g., provider demographics: 1 second lag acceptable)
- Critical data (e.g., member eligibility): Consider read-your-writes or synchronous updates
- Inform users when data may be slightly delayed ("Data as of [timestamp]")

**Example HIPAA-Compliant Command Handler**:

```csharp
public class UpdateMemberDemographicsCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<UpdateMemberDemographicsCommand, CommandResult>
{
    private readonly WriteDbContext _writeDb;
    private readonly IEventPublisher _eventPublisher;
    private readonly IAuditLogger _auditLogger;
    private readonly IAuthorizationService _authz;

    public async Task<CommandResult> Handle(
        UpdateMemberDemographicsCommand command,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        // 1. Authorization check (HIPAA Access Control)
        var authResult = await _authz.AuthorizeAsync(
            User, command, "UpdateMemberDemographics");

        if (!authResult.Succeeded)
        {
            await _auditLogger.LogAccessDeniedAsync(
                User.Identity.Name,
                "UpdateMemberDemographics",
                command.MemberId,
                "Insufficient permissions");

            return CommandResult.Failure("Access denied");
        }

        using var transaction = await _writeDb.Database.BeginTransactionAsync(cancellationToken);

        try
        {
            var member = await _writeDb.Members.FindAsync(
                new object[] { command.MemberId }, cancellationToken);

            if (member == null)
                return CommandResult.Failure("Member not found");

            // 2. Capture before state for audit (HIPAA Audit Trail)
            var beforeState = new
            {
                member.FirstName,
                member.LastName,
                member.DateOfBirth,
                member.Address
            };

            // 3. Update member (HIPAA Data Integrity)
            member.FirstName = command.FirstName;
            member.LastName = command.LastName;
            member.DateOfBirth = command.DateOfBirth;
            member.Address = command.Address;
            member.LastModified = DateTime.UtcNow;
            member.ModifiedBy = User.Identity.Name;

            await _writeDb.SaveChangesAsync(cancellationToken);

            // 4. Audit log (HIPAA Audit Trail)
            await _auditLogger.LogDataChangeAsync(new AuditEntry
            {
                UserId = User.Identity.Name,
                UserRole = User.Claims.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Type == ClaimTypes.Role)?.Value,
                Action = "UpdateMemberDemographics",
                EntityType = "Member",
                EntityId = member.MemberId.ToString(),
                BeforeState = JsonSerializer.Serialize(beforeState),
                AfterState = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new
                {
                    member.FirstName,
                    member.LastName,
                    member.DateOfBirth,
                    member.Address
                }),
                Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
                IpAddress = HttpContext.Connection.RemoteIpAddress?.ToString(),
                CorrelationId = command.CommandId.ToString()
            });

            // 5. Publish event with PHI encryption (HIPAA Encryption in Transit)
            var evt = new MemberDemographicsUpdatedEvent
            {
                EventId = Guid.NewGuid(),
                MemberId = member.MemberId,
                FirstName = member.FirstName,  // Will be encrypted by event publisher
                LastName = member.LastName,
                DateOfBirth = member.DateOfBirth,
                Address = member.Address,
                Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
                ModifiedBy = User.Identity.Name
            };

            await _eventPublisher.PublishAsync(evt, cancellationToken);
            await transaction.CommitAsync(cancellationToken);

            return CommandResult.Success(member.MemberId);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            await transaction.RollbackAsync(cancellationToken);

            await _auditLogger.LogErrorAsync(
                User.Identity.Name,
                "UpdateMemberDemographics",
                command.MemberId.ToString(),
                ex.Message);

            throw;
        }
    }
}
