#### Event Schema Versioning

Events are the contract between write and read sides. Schema changes must be managed carefully:

**Versioning Strategy**:
```csharp
// Version 1
public class MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventV1 : DomainEvent
{
    public Guid MemberId { get; set; }
    public string FirstName { get; set; }
    public string LastName { get; set; }
}

// Version 2 - Add field
public class MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventV2 : DomainEvent
{
    public Guid MemberId { get; set; }
    public string FirstName { get; set; }
    public string LastName { get; set; }
    public string MiddleName { get; set; }  // New field - optional
}

// Event upcaster for projection services
public class MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventUpcaster
{
    public MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventV2 Upcast(MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventV1 v1)
    {
        return new MemberDemographicsUpdatedEventV2
        {
            MemberId = v1.MemberId,
            FirstName = v1.FirstName,
            LastName = v1.LastName,
            MiddleName = null  // Default for legacy events
        };
    }
}
```

**Change Compatibility Matrix**:

| Change Type | Backward Compatible? | Forward Compatible? | Strategy |
|-------------|---------------------|---------------------|----------|
| **Add optional field** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | Safe - projections ignore unknown fields |
| **Add required field** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes | Publish new event type, update projections, migrate |
| **Remove field** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | Deprecate field, remove from projections first, then publisher |
| **Rename field** | ❌ No | ❌ No | Publish both old and new fields during transition period |
| **Change field type** | ❌ No | ❌ No | Publish new event type, dual-write during migration |

